         "step": 1,
         "text": "Substituting \\( x = -1 \\) and \\( f(-1) = 3 \\) into the relation gives \\( f^{\\prime}(-1) = -3 \\).",
         "mathjson": -3,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99027",
         "rule_named": "evaluate the relation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule, \\( f^{\\prime\\prime}(x) = f(x) + x f^{\\prime}(x) \\), so \\( f^{\\prime\\prime}(-1) = 6 \\).",
         "mathjson": 6,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99022",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Dividing each value by the matching factorial, the polynomial is \\( 3 - 3 \\left(x + 1\\right) + 3 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} \\).",
